// The effectsfx package: effects at the standard of the best shooters, defined as data and
// drawn by the GPU. A program reaches it with 'import effectsfx'. It sits beside 'vfx' (which
// keeps its stateless emitters) and over 'gpu', 'render' (the lights, the image-quality
// passes and their decals) and 'noise'.
//
// WHAT IT HAS, each with its method named:
//
// - GPU PARTICLES (particles.cone, particlesim.slang, particledraw.slang). A pool of
//   particles that lives on the GPU as a ring buffer, simulated by a compute kernel a
//   frame, spawned from batches the CPU lists, with forces (gravity, drag, wind, curl
//   noise) and COLLISION WITH THE DEPTH BUFFER (screen-space collision) so sparks skitter
//   and bounce across whatever the scene drew; a ground plane catches what the depth
//   buffer cannot see. Drawn as velocity-stretched additive sparks and as soft, sun-lit
//   smoke puffs.
// - FLIPBOOK EXPLOSIONS (flipbook.cone, flipbook.slang). A fireball that billows and rolls
//   into smoke, BAKED ON THE GPU AT START-UP from a procedural volumetric model (ray
//   marched fBm-displaced density with a cooling temperature, shaded for emission and
//   soot) into an atlas of frames, then played as camera-facing billboards with frame
//   blending: a volumetric look at the cost of a textured quad.
// - HEAT DISTORTION AND SHOCKWAVES (distort.cone, distort.slang). Refraction sprites that
//   read a copy of the frame and offset where they read: a ring that sweeps outward
//   (a sphere's silhouette), a rising shimmer.
// - POINT LIGHTS (lights.cone). An effect's flash and glow as lights in render's clustered
//   light set, each with an intensity curve over time.
// - MESH DEBRIS (debris.cone). Chunks of any mesh thrown ballistically, bouncing and
//   coming to rest, drawn through render's draw list.
// - IMPACT DECALS (decals.cone). A scorch texture made from a few numbers, laid with
//   render's box-projected decals and faded with time.
// - A CAMERA-SHAKE HOOK (shake.cone). Trauma, Eiserloh's model: shake grows with the
//   square of a trauma that decays, driven by smooth noise, with distance falloff.
// - A SMALL-GRID FIRE AND SMOKE FLUID (fluid.cone, fluid.slang, fluidvolume.slang). Stable
//   fluids on the GPU (semi-Lagrangian advection, a Jacobi pressure projection, buoyancy,
//   vorticity confinement) in a box of about 90 thousand cells, drawn by ray marching: a flame
//   that licks and a plume that eddies. It is state on the GPU, driven by 'step' and 'render'.
// - A HALF-RESOLUTION LAYER (lowres.cone). Smoke, flipbooks and the fluid volume at a quarter of the
//   fragments ('halfResolution'), for the integrated GPU.
// - EFFECTS AS DATA (effect.cone). An 'Effect' is lists of layers of those kinds; an
//   'EffectPlayer' registers effects once and plays any number of them, each an event
//   (an effect, a seed, a start and a placement) the way vfx's event is. No effect is
//   written in code; the examples' effects are values.
//
// A FRAME, with render's Renderer, Post and ImageFx (the image-quality driver whose
// scene half leaves the depth for the effects):
//
//   fx.renderScene(&mut device, &mut encoder, &mut renderer, &mut post, &camera, &light, &list);
//   player.update(&mut device, &mut encoder, &mut renderer, &fx, &mut post, &camera, now, dt, &mut list);
//   fx.renderFinish(&mut device, &mut encoder, &mut renderer, &mut post, &list, &target);
//
// Its files are one module, and only this one, the root, imports.

mod effectsfx;

import libc;
import geomath use *;
import collections use *;
import noise use pcg4d, toUnit, toSigned, UVec4, value2, fbm2;
import mesh use Mesh;
import gpu use *;
import render use *;
